  "worksheets": {"CardNTorsion":{"slug":"CardNTorsion","title":"the card `n`-torsion theorem","tagline":"`#E[n](K) = n²`","subject":"the card `n`-torsion theorem: the `n`-torsion of an elliptic curve over an algebraically closed field has `n²` elements","intro":"The port's main theorem as the compiler sees it: over an algebraically closed field, the `n`-torsion of an elliptic curve has `n²` elements. The worksheet unpacks the statement, the fibre count, and the division-polynomial engine behind it.","reads":"FLTForHuman/Elliptic/TorsionCard.lean, the port of the pinned FLT P2M/Sol/S_WeierstrassCurve_card_torsion_of_isAlgClosed.lean, re-exported at Theorems/Thm_WeierstrassCurve_card_torsion_of_isAlgClosed.lean:8-9 <https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b3/Theorems/Thm_WeierstrassCurve_card_torsion_of_isAlgClosed.lean#L8-L9>","status":"open","date":"2026-10-14","file":"lean/play/CardNTorsion.lean","card_count":121,"seed_count":47},"DivisionPolynomials":{"slug":"DivisionPolynomials","title":"the division polynomials","tagline":"ψ, Ψ, ΨSq, Φ, φ and the EDS under them","subject":"the division polynomials of a Weierstrass curve, and the elliptic divisibility sequence (EDS) layer that generates them","intro":"Companion to `CardNTorsion.lean`, which reads the *point* side of the same story; this worksheet reads the *polynomial* side: what `W.Φ`, `W.Ψ`, `W.ΨSq`, `W.ψ` are, which recurrence generates them, and what the EDS vocabulary buys. The mathematics is written up in `math/025-elliptic-nets-division-polynomials-and-the-invariant.md`.","reads":"FLTForHuman/Elliptic/Omega.lean, the top of the EDS cone: it imports Net → RedInvar → Complement → EllSequence → EDS → DivisionPolynomial, and hence mathlib's AlgebraicGeometry/EllipticCurve/DivisionPolynomial/Basic.lean and NumberTheory/EllipticDivisibilitySequence.lean","status":"open","date":"2026-10-15","file":"lean/play/DivisionPolynomials.lean","card_count":182,"seed_count":107}},
